0 Author: BRICK project
0 !BRICK_STATE {"schema_version":3,"status":"instruction_reconstruction_in_progress","model":"Triceratops fossil reconstruction","reference_set":"LEGO 77985","reference_url":"https://www.lego.com/cdn/product-assets/product.bi.core.pdf/6649865.pdf","manual_files":["6649865.pdf"],"progress_note":"Latest origin/main 21bae1a integrated; Triceratops candidate crosswalk from 8ca6bf3 remains current. MPD has 161 root-reachable physical instance records, including explicitly isolated local subassemblies. Steps4–6 remain display-base/rock, separate from fossil skull. Steps247/249/278 use latest inventory corrections; step4 grid, step249 parallel 6541 holes, 6141 insertion, and 25264 cap interfaces, and step278 link geometry were recalculated. Step279 has a partial 32056-to-47905 body-port candidate at zero centerline residual; the whole skull pose remains provisional. Steps250–277 are local candidate fragments; 280–290 branches remain independent with hinge/placement uncertainty. Steps291–292 add no pieces; 294 plaque/minifigure excluded. Instance records are not a completed BOM.","piece_count":161,"unique_sale_skus":7,"listed_retail_parts_cost_cny":"0.95","cost_scope":"Not totaled; candidate mappings only.","target_dimensions_cm":{"length":null,"height":null,"width":null},"reference_geometry_bounds_cm":{"length":null,"height":null,"width":null},"support_count":0,"support_verification":"Not assessed.","validation":{"instruction_scope":"Current official 6649865.pdf. Step4 18980-to-60474 projected grid registration is three points; the proxy underside lock is absent. Step249 sandwich core is recalculated from p.137 substeps: parallel 6541 axes, 6141 sidewall insertion, and 25264-to-stud interval registration. Step278 current 32056/92907/61332 local geometry and shaft intervals are recorded. Step279 includes one candidate body-side fit from the free 32056 axlehol4 line to the 247 47905 +Z stud; the full skull pose remains provisional because the skull-local connection is not assembled.","placements":"Step4: 18980 DAT stud grid projects onto 60474 proxy points (120,-10),(120,10),(140,10), with an 8-LDU layer offset; no physical underside sockets are modeled. Step249: p.137 substeps 2–3 show the two 6541 hole axes parallel. The reversed 6141s place underside tube features in the +Z side ports and outward studs along +Z; the nominal stud span is z=10..14. The 25264 DAT anti-stud span maps to z=10..14 at candidate origin z=5. Centerline/nominal intervals register; mold tolerance and cap azimuth remain unverified. Step278: 32056 DAT lines (0,-5,0) axlehol4 and (0,-5,20) round peghole match the 92907 +X ports at y=20,z=0/-20; the web meets x=20, and 61332 spans x=0..40, nominally through block x=0..20 and 10 LDU into web x=20..30. Section compatibility remains candidate-level. Step279 candidate: free 32056 axlehol4 line point (40,-5,0) maps to 47905 +Z stud center [0,10,10], axes oppose, residual 0 LDU and nominal stud projection 4 LDU. Whole skull pose remains provisional.","catalog_and_asset_references":"origin/main 21bae1a is integrated. The 77985 reviewed_step_candidates are the latest set-specific crosswalk from 8ca6bf3; newer main inventory changes cover T-rex and do not revise 77985. Shared manifest now has 1037 files; official part references resolve. GoBricks SKU mapping remains unverified.","full_connection_graph":"Step278 sequence p.148 attaches the 92907 end to the skull; two 61332 pins internally join the block to two 32056 line features. Step279 adds no pieces. The free 32056 axlehol4 end is tentatively matched to the 247 47905 side stud by centerline/axis fit; this uses only one body-side port and does not prove the hidden side, visual pose or full skull-local transform. Step249 is a distinct body support candidate; p.137 step2–3 show parallel hole axes, and step4–5 register one 6141/25264 cap chain per side-hole port.","exact_mesh_collision":"unverified_open_surface_probe_ambiguous","physical_build":"not_tested","mesh_collision_note":"No new Boolean or BVH collision pass is claimed for the revised DAT candidates. Earlier probes on 32140/32184/11214 and 43093/62462 are superseded and invalid for current geometry; their non-manifold failures do not validate this fit. New axis/position calculations are reported separately from collision status.","surface_collision_note":"No surface-intersection check was rerun on unchanged meshes. Earlier open-triangle BVH outputs were ambiguous at intended contacts and belong to withdrawn candidate geometries. Current 18980, 249, 278 and 279 checks are centerline/grid/interval calculations only; surface collision remains unverified.","open_questions":[{"id":"step249-receiver-axis","status":"deferred_user_uncertain_keep_candidates","manual_page":137,"step":249,"candidates":["parallel 6541 hole axes","orthogonal 6541 hole axes"],"evidence":"The user answered to keep parallel/orthogonal possibilities because the hidden face is unclear. Step249 side-hole direction does not alone resolve the current step279 candidate; the step247 +Z 47905 stud is a single-port feature candidate and the whole torso/skull transform remains provisional.","needed":"Do not repeat the question. Retain this axis ambiguity until a later reverse view or confirmed mating part distinguishes it."}]},"nodes":{"skull-torso-link":{"origin":"92907 local origin; page148 sequence identifies this as skull-side. Step279 candidate transform maps the free 32056 axlehol4 line to the 247 receiver stud; the whole skull local frame is absent.","step278_parts":["32056.dat","92907.dat","61332.dat x2"],"withdrawn_assumptions":["32140/32184/11214 identities","40-LDU old port pitch","shared +Y hole axis","+20 LDU old mating translation","step247 6541 receiver fit"],"verified_local_geometry":{"crossblock_port_lines":[{"point":[0,20,0],"axis":[1,0,0]},{"point":[0,20,-20],"axis":[1,0,0]}],"liftarm_transform":{"translation":[25,20,0],"matrix":[0,1,0,1,0,0,0,0,-1]},"pin_axis":[1,0,0],"pin_positions":[[20,20,0],[20,20,-20]],"pin_span_each":[0,40],"crossblock_x_span":[0,20],"liftarm_x_span":[20,30],"nominal_pin_insertion_into_liftarm":10,"pin_interface_status":"Hole centerlines and face datum match; 61332 section compatibility with one 32056 axlehol4 and one round peghole is not independently proven.","liftarm_hole_line_points":[{"point":[0,-5,0],"type":"axlehol4","axis":[0,1,0]},{"point":[0,-5,20],"type":"round_peghole","axis":[0,1,0]},{"point":[0,-5,40],"type":"axlehol4","axis":[0,1,0]},{"point":[20,-5,0],"type":"round_peghole","axis":[0,1,0]},{"point":[40,-5,0],"type":"axlehol4","axis":[0,1,0]}]},"current_status":"Step278 local geometry is registered. Page148 attaches the 92907 end to the skull before step279. A partial step279 body-side candidate maps the free 32056 axlehol4 line to the 247 47905 +Z stud with 0-LDU centerline residual, opposed axes, nominal 12-LDU features and 4-LDU projected insertion. The complete skull/body pose and selected receiver side remain provisional.","step279_candidate":{"receiver":"part-0041 47905.dat +Z side stud","receiver_point":[0,10,10],"receiver_axis":[0,0,1],"link_port":"part-0037 32056.dat free axlehol4","part_local_line_point":[40,-5,0],"link_local_point_after_step278":[20,60,0],"link_local_axis_after_step278":[1,0,0],"relative_translation":[0,-50,30],"relative_rotation":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"centerline_residual_ldu":0,"mating_axis_after_transform":[0,0,-1],"nominal_stud_diameter_ldu":12,"nominal_hole_diameter_ldu":12,"projected_stud_insertion_ldu":4,"status":"candidate_partial_body_port_fit; skull-side datum and overall pose remain provisional"}},"independent-base-280":{"origin":"local datum at center of 2x10 plate, isolated at world X=600 to keep it independent from torso/skull fragments","parts":[{"id":"part-0052","part":"3832.dat","role":"2x10 tan base plate; shape/stud count confirmed"},{"id":"part-0053","part":"50340.dat","role":"1x2 dual-finger hinge shape candidate; direction provisional"},{"id":"part-0054","part":"3623.dat","role":"first 1x3 plate, adjacent base row; placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0055","part":"3623.dat","role":"second 1x3 plate, adjacent base row; placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0056","part":"87079.dat","role":"step282 2x4 tile cover candidate; placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0057","part":"3023b.dat","role":"step283 1x2 plate row; position provisional"},{"id":"part-0058","part":"3700.dat","role":"step283 1x2 Technic brick with two holes; row/orientation provisional"},{"id":"part-0059","part":"50340.dat","role":"step283 first dual-finger hinge candidate; direction provisional"},{"id":"part-0060","part":"50340.dat","role":"step283 second dual-finger hinge candidate; direction provisional"},{"id":"part-0061","part":"3021.dat","role":"step284 2x3 plate; identity supported by six-stud callout and official shape, placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0062","part":"3022.dat","role":"step284 2x2 plate; identity supported by four-stud callout/underside and official shape, placement provisional"},{"id":"part-0063","part":"1762.dat","role":"step285 first of two 2x2 double-curved slope candidates; shape/quantity candidate, transform provisional"},{"id":"part-0064","part":"1762.dat","role":"step285 second double-curved slope candidate; paired row provisional"},{"id":"part-0065","part":"30355.dat","role":"step286 large studded triangular wing panel; official 6x12 left shape candidate, side/hinge transform provisional"},{"id":"part-0066","part":"30356.dat","role":"step286 mirrored 6x12 right wing panel candidate; exact callout mold allocation and hinge transform provisional"},{"id":"part-0067","part":"67142.dat","role":"step287 left 5x13 curved perforated panel candidate; outer edge registration provisional"},{"id":"part-0068","part":"68196.dat","role":"step287 right 5x13 curved perforated panel candidate; mirrored fit and hole engagement provisional"},{"id":"part-0069","part":"24299.dat","role":"step288 one of the counted pair on corresponding side; official handed wing shape candidate, precise contact provisional"},{"id":"part-0070","part":"24299.dat","role":"step288 one of the counted pair on corresponding side; official handed wing shape candidate, precise contact provisional"},{"id":"part-0071","part":"24307.dat","role":"step288 one of the counted pair on corresponding side; official handed wing shape candidate, precise contact provisional"},{"id":"part-0072","part":"24307.dat","role":"step288 one of the counted pair on corresponding side; official handed wing shape candidate, precise contact provisional"}],"status":"independent subassembly draft; steps 280–288 represented; outer wedge positions remain provisional"},"base-extension-289-local":{"origin":"center datum of the brown 3666 1x6 plate; independent step289 plate pair, held at world X=900 until its attachment point on the main base is measured","parts":[{"id":"part-0073","part":"3666.dat","role":"step289 brown 1x6 base; six-stud row confirmed by callout"},{"id":"part-0074","part":"3020.dat","role":"step289 tan 2x4 cap; four studs align to one row of 3666, row offset provisional"},{"id":"part-0075","part":"3023b.dat","role":"Printed p155 step289 callout: tan 1x2 plate by two-stud count. Placed at the free end of the local 3666/3020 pair; row/overlap provisional."},{"id":"part-0076","part":"50340.dat","role":"Printed p155 step289 callout: 1x2 modified hinge plate candidate. Local branch placement follows the successive substep, but finger direction and connection surface are provisional. Official DAT axis candidate +Z at y=2; step291–292 movement supports articulation but exact engagement/fold angle is unresolved."},{"id":"part-0077","part":"77850.dat","role":"Printed p155 step289: rounded-end reddish-brown 1x3 plate candidate, based on three-stud icon. Placed above the hinge area; exact part identity and row are provisional."},{"id":"part-0078","part":"4032a.dat","role":"Printed p155 step289 final callout: round tan 2x2 plate candidate, aligned above the brown round-end element. Center-hole identity and exact vertical layer remain unverified."}],"status":"steps289 substeps 1–5 represented locally; panel-to-base contact and final platform transform unverified","hinge_axis_check":{"part_candidate":"50340.dat","local_axis":[0,0,1],"local_axis_line_point":[0,2,0],"finger_centers_z":[-16,16],"current_instance_rotation":"identity; local +Z preserved","manual_evidence":"steps291–292 show adjacent panels rotating about the hinge row","status":"axis candidate registered; mating half/knuckles, pivot co-location, insertion and final angle unverified"}},"base-extension-290-local":{"origin":"center of brown 3666 1x6 local plate; separate branch on the opposing platform side, world X=1200 only as isolation placement","parts":[{"id":"part-0079","part":"3666.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290: six-stud reddish-brown 1x6 plate, local datum for opposite extension branch."},{"id":"part-0080","part":"3020.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290: eight-stud tan 2x4 plate aligned to one 3666 stud row; exact row offset diagram-based."},{"id":"part-0081","part":"3023b.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290: tan 1x2 plate candidate at the branch tip; local attachment row provisional."},{"id":"part-0082","part":"50340.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290 modified hinge plate shape candidate; finger direction and contact surface provisional. Official DAT axis candidate +Z at y=2; step291–292 movement supports articulation but exact engagement/fold angle is unresolved."},{"id":"part-0083","part":"77850.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290 three-stud rounded-end reddish-brown plate candidate, placed in the illustrated hinge stack provisionally."},{"id":"part-0084","part":"4032a.dat","role":"Printed p156 step290 round 2x2 plate/cap candidate on the local hinge stack; bore identity and depth unresolved."}],"status":"partial local subassembly; step290 perforated left/right panels are held only at their unresolved branch contacts while the plate/hook base proceeds","hinge_axis_check":{"part_candidate":"50340.dat","local_axis":[0,0,1],"local_axis_line_point":[0,2,0],"finger_centers_z":[-16,16],"current_instance_rotation":"identity; local +Z preserved","manual_evidence":"steps291–292 show adjacent panels rotating about the hinge row","status":"axis candidate registered; mating half/knuckles, pivot co-location, insertion and final angle unverified"}},"torso-extension-250-local":{"origin":"center of official 3710 plate; long axis local X, kept independent from body receiver until the stud row is visible","root_transform_status":"diagram-matched local extension; root X=1600 is only an isolation coordinate; body contact transform unresolved"},"torso-detail-251-local":{"origin":"center of the small step251 callout grouping, isolated from the torso and step250 fragment","root_transform_status":"callout silhouette/count placed locally; part facing, pin/peghole assignment and body transform remain provisional pending step252/253 and opposite-side views","step252":{"part":"50950.dat","position":[0,-24,10],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"evidence":"3x1 footprint and 11458 20-LDU stud pitch align after a quarter turn","status":"shape registration provisional; mold identity/insertion unverified","vertical_datum":{"50950_dat_bottom_y":24,"instance_y":-24,"resulting_bottom_y":0,"11458_top_datum_y":0,"nominal_face_gap_ldu":0,"status":"height registration checked; stud/recess engagement depth and mold identity unverified"}}},"torso-side-253-local":{"origin":"center axis of the 4032a 2x2 round plate; local +Y is the through axlehole axis","root_transform_status":"confirmed internal stud-pitch registration to 3023b; external torso-side placement and facing unresolved"},"torso-side-254-local":{"origin":"center axis of the second 4032a candidate; same internal interface as step253","root_transform_status":"internal pair registered; opposite-side transform is deferred because the view-turn icon does not encode a part transform"},"torso-rib-256-local":{"origin":"right-angle intersection datum of the two 3710 plates; fragment isolated at root X=2400","root_transform_status":"steps256–258 have a diagram-based local L layout; step255 corner subassembly remains unplaced, and neither inter-arm locking nor body transform is asserted"},"torso-detail-259-local":{"origin":"6541 hole-center datum; local +Z is the transverse hole axis and +Y is vertical","root_transform_status":"side 2736 candidate axis and span fit are registered; top brick/stud row is diagram-based; spacer stack withheld pending part identification"},"step247-249-candidate-review":{"step247":{"parts":["47905.dat","6141.dat","6141.dat"],"supersedes":["6541.dat","6577.dat","6577.dat"],"basis":"6649865.pdf p.136 callout; two black round plates stack below the black brick with opposite-side studs.","status":"shape and callout consistent; local stack heights follow 8-LDU plate DAT spacing; receiving contact remains provisional."},"step249":{"parts":["3023b.dat x2","6541.dat x2","6141.dat x2","25264.dat x2"],"core_registration":"p.137 step2–3 show two adjacent 6541 bricks on the 3023b plate pair with both side holes facing the same way; local DAT hole axes are parallel.","6141_contact":"Each 6141 is reversed from the earlier draft: its underside tube enters the +Z 6541 side port, while its top stud points +Z. The DAT interval is registered into the port; exact molded friction remains provisional.","25264_contact":"The p.137 step4–5 cap is placed on the outward 6141 stud. Official 25264 anti-stud tube y=[-9,-5], rotated local Y to -Z and translated z=5, overlaps the 6141 outward stud interval z=[10,14] by nominal 4 LDU. Rotational detail and real tolerances remain unverified.","status":"Diagram sequence and centerline/nominal interval registration are supported; exact molded pressure-fit and step249-to-body transform remain provisional."}},"early-display-steps-4-10":{"scope_correction":"Steps 4-10 are display-base/rock-and-plant assembly, not fossil skull construction.","step4":{"part":"18980.dat","color":"Dark Tan / LDraw 28","replaces":"50950.dat","placement":"18980 stud row aligned to base-end row x=40..140,z=±10; green 60474 round platform is one plate layer above. Exact page-11 contact remains provisional."},"step5":{"parts":["24316.dat x2","32064a.dat x2","3713.dat x2 shown in this local callout"],"replaces":["4519.dat and 2780.dat candidates"],"geometry":"32064a DAT local hole center [0,10,10], local axis -Z. Its transform maps center to [50,-38,0]/[110,-38,0] and axis to world -X. 24316 local shaft axis +X is antiparallel on the same centerline; 3713 local bore +Y maps +X.","rechecked_but_retained":["3700.dat step-3 technic bricks remain in the earlier assembly; 32064a.dat is a separate step-5 addition."]},"step6":{"parts":["3005.dat","28192.dat x2"],"replaces":["false fossil-skull grouping","24299.dat","24307.dat"],"status":"brick/slope display formation; local shape match, exact contacts provisional."},"step10":{"parts":["68211.dat","4367.dat","22667.dat"],"replaces":["24855.dat","37695.dat","24866.dat"],"status":"stem, white flower and dark-azure cherry from callout; plant-local contacts provisional."}}},"joints":[{"id":"joint-skull-anterior-torso","type":"technic_pin_link_to_technic_mount","from":"completed_skull_rear_connector","to":"anterior_torso_technic_mount","evidence":{"manual_file":"6649865.pdf","printed_pages":[148,149],"steps":[278,279]},"connection_status":"candidate_partial_body_port_fit_full_skull_pose_provisional","connector_parts_status":"Step278 92907 side is attached to the skull in the p.148 sequence; internal pins/32056 geometry are registered. A body-side 32056/47905 feature fit is represented as a candidate with computed axes and insertion span.","relative_transform_status":"Partial body-port candidate translation [0,-50,30], rotation [[0,0,1],[0,1,0],[-1,0,0]] maps the free 32056 axlehol4 line onto the 47905 +Z stud, with 0-LDU centerline residual and opposed axes. Whole skull pose remains provisional.","reason":"At p.148 the 92907 end is attached to the skull before step279, so the free 32056 end is tested against the body. The 47905 DAT side stud at [0,10,10], +Z has nominal 12-LDU diameter. The selected 32056 axlehol4 line maps to that center and -Z axis, with 4-LDU projected stud insertion. This is shape-function compatible, but the hidden manual view does not confirm receiver side or whole skull pose.","connector_candidates":["32056.dat","92907.dat","61332.dat x2"]}],"instances":[{"id":"part-0001","group":"stand","part":"4282.dat","gobricks_id":"517","sku":"GDS-517-031","color":19,"position":[0,0,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Step 1 tan 2x16 base; datum center."},{"id":"part-0002","group":"stand","part":"36840.dat","gobricks_id":"1567","sku":"GDS-1567-072","color":72,"position":[-140,0,0],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Step 1 gray inverted bracket near one end; X approximate from diagram."},{"id":"part-0003","group":"stand","part":"3023b.dat","gobricks_id":"502","sku":"GDS-502-081","color":70,"position":[-100,-8,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Step 2 first reddish-brown 1x2 plate; diagram placement."},{"id":"part-0004","group":"stand","part":"3023b.dat","gobricks_id":"502","sku":"GDS-502-081","color":70,"position":[-80,-8,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Step 2 second reddish-brown 1x2 plate; stud locations provisional."},{"id":"part-0005","group":"stand","part":"54200.dat","gobricks_id":"833","sku":"GDS-833-081","color":70,"position":[-60,-8,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"candidate_unverified","placement_note":"Manual printed page 11 step 3; inventory visible, exact mold candidate and stud placement provisional."},{"id":"part-0006","group":"stand","part":"36840.dat","gobricks_